// OpenWar3 override — strings the game has no key for.
//
// Layered onto `UI\FrameDef\GlobalStrings.fdf` (src/overrides/index.ts), which is where every
// other label on these two screens comes from. Blizzard never shipped a second melee AI, and
// its own observing is something other PEOPLE do to a hosted game, so there is no COMPUTERPLUS_*
// to reuse and nothing that says "sit this one out and watch": these keys are ours, and they
// follow the file's own naming so they read as part of the same table.
//
// The three "Computer+ (…)" labels a SLOT MENU shows are deliberately NOT here — they are in
// src/ui/playerSlots.ts beside the classic ones they mirror, because the owner line of a hover
// tooltip asks for them mid-match, with no FDF library in scope.

StringList {
    // Custom Game → Advanced Options. Sits in the same column as COLON_LOCK_TEAMS
    // ("Lock Teams:") and COLON_ADV_SHARED_CONTROL ("Full Shared Unit Control:"), and is no
    // longer than the latter.
    COLON_COMPUTER_PLUS         "Computer+ (Improved AI):",

    // ...and the row the game's own COLON_OBSERVERS ("Observers:") had. That one offered four
    // ways for other people to watch a HOSTED game and could never be anything but "No
    // Observers" on this screen; this one is about the person sitting at this machine, so it
    // is a mode rather than a guest list.
    COLON_OBSERVER_MODE         "Observer Mode:",

    // Options → Gameplay, directly under AUTOSAVE_REPLAY ("Automatically Save Replays").
    COMPUTER_PLUS_DEFAULT       "Use Computer+ as default AI",

    // The LAN game lobby's TEAM menu, under Full Observers: the entry that moves a player onto
    // the Observers bench, and what a watcher's row reads in that column. The game names the
    // force with a colon (COLON_OBSERVERS "Observers:") and the mode by its full phrase
    // (FULL_OBSERVERS); the bare word a menu entry wants is nowhere in its table.
    OBSERVERS_TEAM              "Observers",

    // Options, Gameplay panel: the row this engine adds directly UNDER "Always show Health
    // Bars" (issue #141). Punctuated like every other pulldown label on this screen --
    // COLON_RESOLUTION "Resolution:" is the row it is built to look like -- and its two
    // entries are named the way the Video panel's are (LOW_MODELS, HIGH_PARTICLES): the
    // value, then the row it belongs to, because GlobalStrings has no generic word for
    // either of them.
    COLON_HEALTHBARS            "Healthbars:",
    DEFAULT_HEALTHBARS          "Default",
    TEAM_COLORED_HEALTHBARS     "Team Colored",

    // LAN → Create Game, the row under the map list: which relay the game is announced on
    // (src/overrides/ui/LocalMultiplayerCreate.fdf). The game broadcast its LAN games and never
    // had to ask; the nearest thing in its table is Battle.net's COLON_SELECTED_REALM
    // ("Selected Gateway:"), which names a Blizzard gateway and not a place to put a game.
    COLON_SERVER                "Server:",
    // …and its first entry: this machine's own relay, reachable from the local network only.
    THIS_COMPUTER               "This Computer",
}
